# ── never commit credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These patterns are a safety net, not the primary defence: nothing under these
# names is ever copied into the repo in the first place. They exist so that an
# accidental `cp -R` of a config directory cannot leak a token.
*auth.json
*credentials*
*oauth*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*_rsa
*_ed25519
.env
.env.*
**/.aws/**
**/.ssh/**
**/.kube/**
**/gcloud/**
**/github-copilot/**
**/raycast/config.json

# ── claude code runtime state (never config) ─────────────────────────────────
**/.claude.json
**/history.jsonl
**/sessions/
**/projects/
**/telemetry/
**/shell-snapshots/
**/paste-cache/
**/file-history/
**/daemon*.log
**/daemon*.json
**/*.sqlite
**/stats-cache.json
**/security_warnings_state_*.json
settings.local.json

# ── rendered / generated ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# install.sh writes rendered templates here, outside the repo, but ignore the
# name anyway in case someone points RENDER_DIR inward.
.dotfiles-rendered/
.dotfiles-backup/

# ── noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
